(6753439, 1010927, 119012, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by darkfact:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/> <br/>am I missing something? or is this website just dying? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>considering he cant make use of stock images and has to generate all the images himself, I''d say its a step above "amateur digital art"<br/> <br/>the thing that Gyaban does so well is he doesn''t just throw stuff together like the rest of us do, he has mastered his lighting so it all blends perfectly.<br/> <br/>im not a fan of completely put together shots , but you have to admit he is more than ten steps above most anyone else here as far as hos talents goes, and its not just composite images his creativity and quality are just as stellarand teh effort and time he puts in shows.<br/> <br/>its not sucking up, its giving praise where its due.<br/> <br/>but i digress, Gyaban, this is a fantastic image.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by darkfact:  am I missing something? or is this website just dying?   considering he cant make use of stock images and has to generate all the images himself, I''d say its a step above "amateur digital art" the thing that Gyaban does so well is he doesn''t just throw stuff together like the rest of us do, he has mastered his lighting so it all blends perfectly. im not a fan of completely put together shots , but you have to admit he is more than ten steps above most anyone else here as far as hos talents goes, and its not just composite images his creativity and quality are just as stellarand teh effort and time he puts in shows. its not sucking up, its giving praise where its due. but i digress, Gyaban, this is a fantastic image. ', '2012-04-27 21:39:39.000000', NULL, 0),
